# Aston Martin Rapide four-door saloon, 2010-2020.
#
# The four-door Rapide: the long low fastback saloon on the VH platform,
# built at Magna Steyr from 2010 and at Gaydon from 2012. The Rapide S of
# 2013 is a power and trim variant on the same shell and is not separately
# represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_Rapide
#
# Dimensions 5.019 x 1.928 x 1.359 m, wheelbase 2.990 m.
#
# Shape reference: a blue Rapide on the Galpin stand in true side elevation,
# and a black French car in front and rear three-quarter. The side view is
# one car; the three-quarters another of the same model. The side capture is
# tightly framed and the front wheel is partly obscured.
#
# Colours: grade (a) for the January 2013 Rapide S brochure, which names
# Volcano Red, Morning Frost White and Amethyst Red; Silver Blonde is the
# 2010 launch colour (grade c). No complete UK palette was found. Weights 3,
# 3, 2, 2, total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 296 km/h. Comfort 88/312, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 88: the only
# four-door Aston, with a longer cabin and rear seats. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2010 intro, retires staggered 2036-2039.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-rapide.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-rapide.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-rapide/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the side capture is tightly framed and the rear lamp
# outlines distort at the corners. At 128 px the long four-door fastback, low
# roof and haunches read as a Rapide.


obj=citycar
